{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user has provided a detailed stitch task (#5145) to implement `cmd/dirname` for the go-unix-utils project. The task requires creating two files: `cmd/dirname/main.go` (the dirname utility) and `cmd/dirname/dirname_test.go` (differential tests against the GNU `gdirname` reference binary). The specific scope covers srd016-dirname requirements R1.1 (core dirname behavior extracting directory component), R1.2 (trailing slash stripping before extraction), and R1.3 (return \".\" when path has no slash). The implementation must follow project conventions including SIGPIPE handling, differential testing patterns, copyright headers, and the execution constitution's coding standards.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **Differential testing pattern**: Compare Go binary output against GNU reference binary (`gdirname`) using `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - **SIGPIPE handling**: All cmd/ utilities must call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main\n   - **dirname algorithm**: Strip trailing slashes → check for all-slashes (return \"/\") → check for no slash (return \".\") → remove last component → strip trailing slashes from result → return\n   - **DiffTest struct**: `Name`, `Args`, `Stdin`, `Env`, `WorkDir`, `ExitCode`, `Normalize`, `ExpectedFiles`\n   - **BuildBinary(t, \".\")**: Compiles the cmd package and returns binary path\n   - **exec.LookPath(\"gdirname\")**: Finds reference binary, t.Skip if not found\n   - **LC_ALL=C**: Set in test environment per project convention (handled automatically by testutils.buildEnv)\n   - **NUL-delimited output (-z/--zero flag)**: Output delimiter changes from newline to NUL byte\n   - **Exit codes**: 0 on success, 1 on no args or write error\n\n3. Files an