{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Szk2gmgYH1HVwgZdsvRQnp","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now let me compile my findings. Let me create a comprehensive summary document of all the normalizer patterns found:\n\n## Summary of Error Message Stderr Normalization Patterns\n\nBased on my search of the go-unix-utils repository, here are the error message stderr normalization patterns used in differential tests:\n\n### Core Normalization Infrastructure\nLocated in: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5145/pkg/testutils/difftest.go`\n\n**NormalizeFunc Type Definition (line 28):**\n```go\ntype NormalizeFunc = func([]byte) []byte\n```\n\n**ComposeNormalizers Function (lines 232-239):**\n- Allows chaining multiple normalizers in sequence\n- Applied in order to both stdout and stderr before comparison\n- Can be composed with multiple functions to handle complex transformations\n\n**TimestampNormalizer (lines 57-72):**\n- Pre-built normalizer for handling timestamp variations\n- Matches three common patterns:\n  - Syslog format: `May 13 14:30:00`\n  - ISO format: `2026-05-13 14:30:00`\n  - Time-only: `14:30:00`\n- Replaces all matches with `<TIMESTAMP>` placeholder\n\n### Test File Normalizer Patterns\n\n**1. cmd/basename/basename_test.go (lines 21-26)**\nTwo normalizers for error case testing:\n\n- **discardStdout**: Inline anonymizer that nullifies output\n  ```go\n  discardStdout := testutils.NormalizeFunc(func([]byte) []byte { return nil })\n  ```\n  Used for: `--help` and `--version` tests (stdout differs between binaries)\n\n- **normalizeBinaryName**: Regex-based binary path normalizer\n  ```go\n  binaryNameRe := regexp.MustCompile(`(?:/\\S+/)?g?basename`)\n  normalizeBinaryName := testutils.NormalizeFunc(func(b []byte) []byte {\n      return binaryNameRe.ReplaceAll(b, []byte(\"basename\"))\n  })\n  ```\n  Matches patterns: `basename`, `gbasename`, `/path/basename`, `/path/gbasename`\n  Used for: error tests that include the binary name prefix in stderr\n  Applied to error-no-args (line 109) and error-extra-operand (line 116) tests\n\nThe binary name normalization handles the \"Try 'basename --help'\" line in stderr (from `/cmd/basename/main.go` line 48) where the Go and GNU reference binaries may have different path prefixes.\n\n**2. cmd/true/true_test.go and cmd/false/false_test.go**\nSimple stdout discard pattern:\n- discardStdout used for `--help` and `--version` tests\n\n**3. cmd/dirname/dirname_test.go**\nNo normalizers used (error test for missing operand doesn't include binary name prefix)\n\n**4. cmd/cat/cat_test.go**\nNo normalizers in DiffTest entries\n\n**5. cmd/sponge/sponge_test.go**\nNo normalizers in DiffTest entries (error handling tested with custom functions)\n\n### Key Patterns for Error Message Normalization\n\n1. **Binary Name Prefix Handling**: Use regex to normalize paths and \"g\" prefix\n   - Pattern: `(?:/\\S+/)?g?basename`\n   - Replaces with: canonical name (e.g., \"basename\")\n\n2. **Help Text Variance**: Use `discardStdout` to eliminate diffs in help/version text\n   - Applies to both stdout and stderr in the normalization\n\n3. **Composition**: Multiple normalizers can be chained via `ComposeNormalizers()`\n   - Normalizers applied in order\n   - Each receives and transforms byte output sequentially\n\n4. **Stderr vs Stdout**: Both are normalized identically using the same functions\n   - Applied by `applyNormalizers()` function (line 168-174 in difftest.go)\n\n### Files with Error Normalization Examples\n\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5145/cmd/basename/basename_test.go` - Most comprehensive example\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5145/pkg/testutils/difftest.go` - Framework definition\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5145/pkg/testutils/difftest_test.go` - Framework usage examples\n\nThe most relevant pattern for handling stderr with binary name prefixes (like \"Try 'basename --help'\") is the **normalizeBinaryName** pattern in basename_test.go, which uses regex with optional path prefix and \"g\" prefix matching."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7d7c93bf-288a-41a3-89d1-acd464d604d0","uuid":"1862677b-a998-4ba2-8c6d-744e4a3df660","timestamp":"2026-05-14T11:19:42.790Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In the repo at /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5145, search for how other cmd/ test files handle error message stderr normalization in differential tests. Look for patterns where stderr from the Go binary and reference binary differ (binary name prefix, \"Try --help\" line, etc.). Check cmd/basename/, cmd/yes/, and any other cmd/ test files. I want to see what normalizer functions they use for error-case test entries. Search breadth: medium.","agentId":"a234ae51b44d3a902","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now let me compile my findings. Let me create a comprehensive summary document of all the normalizer patterns found:\n\n## Summary of Error Message Stderr Normalization Patterns\n\nBased on my search of the go-unix-utils repository, here are the error message stderr normalization patterns used in differential tests:\n\n### Core Normalization Infrastructure\nLocated in: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5145/pkg/testutils/difftest.go`\n\n**NormalizeFunc Type Definition (line 28):**\n```go\ntype NormalizeFunc = func([]byte) []byte\n```\n\n**ComposeNormalizers Function (lines 232-239):**\n- Allows chaining multiple normalizers in sequence\n- Applied in order to both stdout and stderr before comparison\n- Can be composed with multiple functions to handle complex transformations\n\n**TimestampNormalizer (lines 57-72):**\n- Pre-built normalizer for handling timestamp variations\n- Matches three common patterns:\n  - Syslog format: `May 13 14:30:00`\n  - ISO format: `2026-05-13 14:30:00`\n  - Time-only: `14:30:00`\n- Replaces all matches with `<TIMESTAMP>` placeholder\n\n### Test File Normalizer Patterns\n\n**1. cmd/basename/basename_test.go (lines 21-26)**\nTwo normalizers for error case testing:\n\n- **discardStdout**: Inline anonymizer that nullifies output\n  ```go\n  discardStdout := testutils.NormalizeFunc(func([]byte) []byte { return nil })\n  ```\n  Used for: `--help` and `--version` tests (stdout differs between binaries)\n\n- **normalizeBinaryName**: Regex-based binary path normalizer\n  ```go\n  binaryNameRe := regexp.MustCompile(`(?:/\\S+/)?g?basename`)\n  normalizeBinaryName := testutils.NormalizeFunc(func(b []byte) []byte {\n      return binaryNameRe.ReplaceAll(b, []byte(\"basename\"))\n  })\n  ```\n  Matches patterns: `basename`, `gbasename`, `/path/basename`, `/path/gbasename`\n  Used for: error tests that include the binary name prefix in stderr\n  Applied to error-no-args (line 109) and error-extra-operand (line 116) tests\n\nThe binary name normalization handles the \"Try 'basename --help'\" line in stderr (from `/cmd/basename/main.go` line 48) where the Go and GNU reference binaries may have different path prefixes.\n\n**2. cmd/true/true_test.go and cmd/false/false_test.go**\nSimple stdout discard pattern:\n- discardStdout used for `--help` and `--version` tests\n\n**3. cmd/dirname/dirname_test.go**\nNo normalizers used (error test for missing operand doesn't include binary name prefix)\n\n**4. cmd/cat/cat_test.go**\nNo normalizers in DiffTest entries\n\n**5. cmd/sponge/sponge_test.go**\nNo normalizers in DiffTest entries (error handling tested with custom functions)\n\n### Key Patterns for Error Message Normalization\n\n1. **Binary Name Prefix Handling**: Use regex to normalize paths and \"g\" prefix\n   - Pattern: `(?:/\\S+/)?g?basename`\n   - Replaces with: canonical name (e.g., \"basename\")\n\n2. **Help Text Variance**: Use `discardStdout` to eliminate diffs in help/version text\n   - Applies to both stdout and stderr in the normalization\n\n3. **Composition**: Multiple normalizers can be chained via `ComposeNormalizers()`\n   - Normalizers applied in order\n   - Each receives and transforms byte output sequentially\n\n4. **Stderr vs Stdout**: Both are normalized identically using the same functions\n   - Applied by `applyNormalizers()` function (line 168-174 in difftest.go)\n\n### Files with Error Normalization Examples\n\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5145/cmd/basename/basename_test.go` - Most comprehensive example\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5145/pkg/testutils/difftest.go` - Framework definition\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5145/pkg/testutils/difftest_test.go` - Framework usage examples\n\nThe most relevant pattern for handling stderr with binary name prefixes (like \"Try 'basename --help'\") is the **normalizeBinaryName** pattern in basename_test.go, which uses regex with optional path prefix and \"g\" prefix matching."}],"totalDurationMs":50082,"totalTokens":56557,"totalToolUseCount":22,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2647,"cache_read_input_tokens":52671,"output_tokens":1235,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2647},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1235,"cache_read_input_tokens":52671,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2647,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2647,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":13,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":9,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
